er/id #uuid "ea224e0a-7ad4-5010-a1a0-80811796a219" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320646/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcf6e2c9-efc7-5e22-8267-79a378a80290" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320646/field-1/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a" :answer-field/choices ["q-320646/field-1/09f471dae983db28c0826657524c52e39160889c30208ec0dd3cf10ef9c2407a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320646" :question/id #uuid "e7ed2198-fcaf-5c09-8a30-b7bdff807930" :question/math-academy-id "q-320646" :question/problem "Expressed in radians, $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/a33ea7c6d1aa7cd7e54376aefb2af4347da59a61ecaabdbf4964d41b9661870a.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320646/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e89b620-641a-5dbf-85f6-ca0f7a2fad80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321120/field-1/e82d86e061b72845f58da66978293b4a67da87c9a3857866b1b1b9d9efd22c47" :answer/id #uuid "af9f3218-99ca-565d-81d4-14796acc9c01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321120/field-1/6568a7f527cbccabebc1d2e55fba33e6d92cc0555602b7b829eae080d006da93" :answer/id #uuid "e123554d-95cb-55ed-a994-e3af99dd131b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321120/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e93f079-34a2-57e1-97c1-34e094e50d21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321120/field-1/e82d86e061b72845f58da66978293b4a67da87c9a3857866b1b1b9d9efd22c47" :answer-field/choices ["q-321120/field-1/e82d86e061b72845f58da66978293b4a67da87c9a3857866b1b1b9d9efd22c47" "q-321120/field-1/6568a7f527cbccabebc1d2e55fba33e6d92cc0555602b7b829eae080d006da93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321120" :question/id #uuid "9e26030d-ff55-5a19-833a-05701f61d0ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-321120" :question/problem "Expressed in radians, $9\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/a33ea7c6d1aa7cd7e54376aefb2af4347da59a61ecaabdbf4964d41b9661870a.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\pi }{3}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\narcsin\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9arcsin\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) & =9(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321120/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321120"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" :answer/id #uuid "13b11ff9-3ec6-5c0f-946a-01c087ac240e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" :answer/id #uuid "3d69014e-1743-5617-8f77-a7e5eb4f20c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "d362583b-059d-5f95-8e73-33e8f2d108e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "7bc28348-7f41-527e-9812-7d23328e0dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "08c73ecb-9cab-55d7-a49a-2acc6a650809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "132d2a0e-ea20-5019-adc4-612fc73aac64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117411/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer-field/choices ["q-117411/selection/a996cecead059c2e05b8ded2ceb60e4e2170a4344e0c20625524ed13b23c6fbe" "q-117411/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" "q-117411/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-117411/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-117411/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117411" :question/id #uuid "02c3cce7-ac66-5194-ad1f-3ef5e81a3aa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-117411" :question/problem "$-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/a33ea7c6d1aa7cd7e54376aefb2af4347da59a61ecaabdbf4964d41b9661870a.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{11\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =(-6)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117411/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320893/field-1/22544889ddd7b88350edc45f9a186dfd49afc624841b8647f5c31e52408e5538" :answer/id #uuid "b7f3cb27-22ab-5228-96a1-c2f3b98c731f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320893/field-1/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer/id #uuid "e0c7a204-1c72-5500-b0aa-a41bfc3f0c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320893/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06cea244-ce37-5115-afe3-ae4fc4bb0319" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320893/field-1/22544889ddd7b88350edc45f9a186dfd49afc624841b8647f5c31e52408e5538" :answer-field/choices ["q-320893/field-1/22544889ddd7b88350edc45f9a186dfd49afc624841b8647f5c31e52408e5538" "q-320893/field-1/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320893" :question/id #uuid "e7893b97-a032-5b93-8a30-5368e64fd2a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-320893" :question/problem "Expressed in degrees, $4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/ca39c4cde40b99fd40a11746a31398d82814268b2df706e3101ee88648c9e2d4.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({315}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${315}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${315}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{315}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-{45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =4\\cdot (-{45}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={-180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320893/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320893"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "c3d487dd-568d-516c-9918-13f64e83cdab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175/selection/0dedc37c1c07b1d3afccefbc2cd1d676db0a66a60d8f6fa588da436c9c06df07" :answer/id #uuid "f373a2d5-dd6d-5278-9205-0f32305859f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "1911c4a4-3223-536d-85c3-f73a25f35638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175/selection/bc1f7595490861f8fa350184b50826541fc7815f7212daefd0983d5cbe822ccc" :answer/id #uuid "8f542216-f7cd-5308-8399-85224c8c45eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175/selection/52b19d1509f380ed3e27038d73c2ce34dca41fd192b1970793b1ede0b8b2080f" :answer/id #uuid "842d42e0-a88e-578b-9d3b-a4a73e6ae0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d73fb4d2-7d88-5d62-9672-0f2ce3eb90fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82175/selection/52b19d1509f380ed3e27038d73c2ce34dca41fd192b1970793b1ede0b8b2080f" :answer-field/choices ["q-82175/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-82175/selection/0dedc37c1c07b1d3afccefbc2cd1d676db0a66a60d8f6fa588da436c9c06df07" "q-82175/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-82175/selection/bc1f7595490861f8fa350184b50826541fc7815f7212daefd0983d5cbe822ccc" "q-82175/selection/52b19d1509f380ed3e27038d73c2ce34dca41fd192b1970793b1ede0b8b2080f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82175" :question/id #uuid "14a18031-c565-5c60-a477-c5a914555373" :question/math-academy-id "q-82175" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({270}^{∘})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${270}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${270}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{270}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-{90}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82175/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320929/field-1/f4ed4b34f4a5de49898377314514d2de061007c11b4d8d545eea74864f386ee8" :answer/id #uuid "95f4084c-9576-5c5a-929f-e32be209ad51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320929/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e306a1-5d36-55a4-9a6e-0eb53ed6bcfc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320929/field-1/f4ed4b34f4a5de49898377314514d2de061007c11b4d8d545eea74864f386ee8" :answer-field/choices ["q-320929/field-1/f4ed4b34f4a5de49898377314514d2de061007c11b4d8d545eea74864f386ee8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320929" :question/id #uuid "d0a553ce-d336-5561-9707-b73587889397" :question/math-academy-id "q-320929" :question/problem "Expressed in degrees, $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({270}^{∘})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${270}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${270}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{270}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)={-90}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320929/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277819/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer/id #uuid "73b1caf6-3bab-5f75-b45c-f39e3bc4c897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277819/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "55466596-4c56-5b42-bcc5-82815c724d32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277819/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer-field/choices ["q-277819/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277819" :question/id #uuid "054b2464-cbfe-5703-9e95-22b9dbe5aff9" :question/math-academy-id "q-277819" :question/problem "Expressed in radians, $4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $1$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where the tangent is positive.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1.\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is an angle in the first quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=4(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-277819/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3878b5fa-fd5e-5984-8516-96ee17bf137b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277819"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "0d1e074c-9743-514c-964c-e3843d44ce75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "cb752986-0b17-5be8-831c-d3a21c158337" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer/id #uuid "a7c25ac4-7f5c-5391-814f-8647ed20d95a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" :answer/id #uuid "c189abac-33eb-538f-a4ab-ce03d93bc620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "bea8a93e-8066-5204-898b-584c99326eb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2670cb3-d48d-5010-9163-e76ac4205fd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117461/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-117461/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-117461/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" "q-117461/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" "q-117461/selection/35d0af53e25a7911f6d08c6d063fcf9231a1273a16a0f7056530d6f5d5dfbdd8" "q-117461/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117461" :question/id #uuid "4591b664-8f5f-503b-bf6e-83fc0b6998fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-117461" :question/problem "$-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\theta <\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\sqrt{3}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the fourth quadrant, where the tangent is negative.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions and the oddness of the tangent function, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is an angle in the fourth quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3}) & =(-2)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficu